  "limits": "Frontend executes actual copied-SQE preparation/publish for fixed and provided paths plus real rejection storage/delivery and engine routing. CONNECT constructor returns controlled NOENT, so its new successful adoption path is not exercised here. Return control fixture additionally executes actual creator authority and copied return validation, exact pool ledger and registered engine-wake path. Pool backing remains controlled as previously stated. Drain fixture composes actual engine get/put/visit/close/wait/collect and actual CONNECT step/release with operation action stack. Handshake install and native poll hooks/protocol destruction remain host boundaries. Earlier cases retain legacy fake engine roots. Action executor uses actual submit, scope abort, owner/program/admission/retirement/selector. Progress step and successful parsed responses remain explicit controlled boundaries in new action cases. Separate external driver pin/root is modeled and asserted. Actual client-mark-dead/progress-abort, transport/session/codec abort, per-owner close and physical operation destructor, final pool-destruction helper, request/FID/pool/CQ transitions. Parsed successful replies remain synthetic; prior preparation regressions never submit. Host native teardown, translation, allocator, image snapshot, ref/engine/wake and physical backing drop boundaries. Earlier preparation/provided cases retain manual fixture destruction; new retirement cases use actual destructor. Final pool helper is called at simulated zero Loom references, not actual retirer. No native READY/frontend/close/concurrency qualification."
